    {
      "id": "ebcc3783-46c7-402c-8199-802d595771dd",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": "#FEF9C2",
        "width": 704,
        "height": 1280,
        "content": "## AI incident classification (Ivanti Neurons for ITSM)\n\nAutomatically triages incidents from **Ivanti Neurons for ITSM** using AI. The workflow reads each incident, includes supported attachments for additional context, selects the most appropriate Service and Category, updates the incident, and adds a short classification note. \n\n### Who's it for\n- IT service desks using **Ivanti Neurons for ITSM**\n- Teams that want to reduce manual incident triage and classification\n- n8n users looking to automate Service and Category assignment with AI\n\n### How it works\n1. **Polling Trigger** retrieves incidents from Ivanti Neurons for ITSM based on the configured filters.\n2. The incident description is cleaned and its related attachments are collected.\n3. Supported attachments are downloaded and passed to the AI Agent for additional context.\n4. **Incident Mapping** prepares the incident data and processes incidents one at a time.\n5. The **AI Agent** selects an appropriate Service, retrieves its available Categories, chooses the best Category, updates the incident, and adds an explanatory note.\n\n\n### Setup\n- Add **Ivanti Neurons for ITSM** credentials.\n  - This workflow uses a community node and therefore requires a **self-hosted n8n instance**.\n- Add your **OpenAI** credentials.\n- Configure the **Polling Trigger**:\n  - Set how often the workflow should check for incidents.\n  - Configure the filters to define **which incidents should be processed**, such as status or other Ivanti fields.\n- Review the **Update Classification** node and confirm that the Service, Category, and classification fields match your Ivanti configuration.\n- Ensure binary passthrough for **Images** and **PDFs** is enabled on the AI Agent.\n\n### Customization\n- Replace the OpenAI model with another compatible chat model.\n- Adjust the polling interval and incident filters.\n- Modify the classification instructions or the note written back to the incident.\n- Change which Ivanti fields are used when selecting incidents for automatic classification.\n\n### Requirements\n- Ivanti Neurons for ITSM verified community node installed in n8n.\n- Valid Ivanti Neurons for ITSM credentials\n- Valid OpenAI credentials\n- An OpenAI-compatible model that supports image and PDF inputs\n\n### Additional info\n- Supported attachment types: images and PDFs only"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
